Z||000034||Gerald||10-09-2001||10:38 PM||||Ok Ive calmed down now. Today I bought a one man brake bleeder and the axel seal I needed.Im going to re bleed all my brakes and see if that helps. I checked my pads less then a thousand km ago and they still had 40%. So thats not the problem. As for the muffler its going to have to wait another 2 weeks. That will take care of the noise. My clutch in brand new( less then 20 km on it) and i didit myself. I guess thats why I was so frustrated at the car. That was my first clutch in any car. Not fun at all. As for the oil leaks theres not alot I can do for now but keep it cleaned to avoid the fire hazard part of the car. I have a friend whos company makes lambo replacas based on fieros so I got 4 rims (hi tech), 120mph gauges including the rally gauges, and various other interier parts that i needed. I may also be getting some racing buckets from him. I have first dibs on the next fiero that gets stripped. Infact I get to strip it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I get any parts that i strip for free. I will be selling alot of things. OK this post is long enuf. So im done for now.<P>Oh yamy front facia is in bad shape and i want to replace it. I  want to maybe use a 84-86 coupe facia. I like them?????? Just got to paint the pads and fill in the rub strip. ( my cars a 87) Is it going to be a pain to install or should it go on nice and easy.<BR>Thanx||||reg||6
Z||000035||AutoXdbdragSE||10-09-2001||11:14 PM||||Gtmike, Yay, there's that V-6 or nothing attitude i get from most fiero owners..  <P>How unlikely is it.. i have a fresh 10,000 mile .20 over 2.5, that factory put out 135 lbft of torque, no cat, and slightly advanced timing, on 4.10 gearing.<BR>a fiero GT has a v-6 with 160lbft of torque, only 30 more, and is running on 3.23 gears.. so it it entierly likely i would at least keep up with one until 40... an auto is even more likely i could give it a run.. and as a cocky v-6 owner, how hard would you try if you pulled up to a bone stock 84 2m4.. i mean they don't have stickers showing off the 4.10 muncie.. so they think guarenteed win.. then i get them till 40... when i shift to third then horsepower takes over, and i wave good by to v-6... but it is  entirely possible that a 4-cyl can keep up with a gt.. just under the right conditions||||reg||1
